{
  "_comment": "Fault injection in the hook gates (chaosGate.ts, intutic_clawde/gate/chaos.py and every hook gate that emits them). A valid case is a plan and a run of calls, each with the decision governance made before any fault; replayed in order against a fresh events file, each call ends as `outcome` (with the refusal `reason` when a fault applies: `deny`, or `hold` for a call a permission fault holds), and the events file holds `events` in order: each line also carries `ts` (ISO-8601), the plan's `runId` and `component` gate. An invalid case is a plan (base64url-encoded by the runner) or a raw environment value that every gate refuses to load, failing closed; every invalid plan is also one ChaosPlanSchema rejects, and every valid one one it accepts. A call's `input` is its tool input (a runner that cannot send one sends a harmless input of its own for the tool, the same every time): two calls with the same tool and input are the same call, so the second is the retry of the first when it was held. A call's `advanceS` moves the clock that many seconds forward before it is made: a runner moves the modification time of every file in `<events>.gate-counters/` back by that much.",
